.. py:module:: simplebench.cli

   CLI script support for SimpleBench.


.. py:function:: main(benchmark_cases: Optional[Sequence[Case]] = None, *, argv: Optional[list[str]] = None, extra_args: Optional[list[str]] = None) -> ExitCode
   :module: simplebench.cli

   Main entry point for running benchmarks via a command-line interface.

   This function is responsible for setting up the command-line interface,
   parsing arguments, and executing the benchmark cases.

   :deco:`~simplebench.decorators.benchmark` (``@simplebench.benchmark``) decorated benchmark cases
   are automatically included and added to the list of benchmark cases passed to this function.

   Usage:
       This function serves as the main entry point for running benchmarks.

   :param benchmark_cases: A Sequence of SimpleBench.Case instances to be benchmarked.
   :param argv: A list of command-line arguments to parse. If None, defaults to sys.argv.
   :param extra_args: Additional command-line arguments to include.
   :return: An enum :class:`ExitCode` which has an integer exit code value
       - ``ExitCode.SUCCESS`` (0) on success
       - ``ExitCode.RUNTIME_ERROR`` (1) runtime errors during execution.
       - ``ExitCode.CLI_ARGUMENTS_ERROR`` (2) for errors during CLI argument processing
       - ``ExitCode.KEYBOARD_INTERRUPT`` (3) if interrupted by keyboard interrupt


