.. py:module:: simplebench.reporters.reporter.config

   Base reporter configuration class.


.. py:class:: ReporterConfig(*, name: str, description: str, metrics: frozenset[~simplebench.enums.metric.Metric], targets: frozenset[~simplebench.enums.target.Target], default_targets: frozenset[~simplebench.enums.target.Target], formats: frozenset[~simplebench.enums.format.Format], choices: ~simplebench.reporters.choices.choices_conf.ChoicesConf, file_suffix: str, file_unique: bool, file_append: bool, subdir: str)
   :module: simplebench.reporters.reporter.config

   Bases: :py:class:`object`

   Immutable, attribute-based base configuration for a Reporter.

   This frozen dataclass serves as the foundation for all specific reporter
   configuration classes (e.g., :class:`~simplebench.reporters.rich_table.config.RichTableConfig`).
   It defines the common data structure and centralizes the validation of all parameters required
   by reporters.

   The ``metrics``, ``targets``, and ``formats`` parameters act as master lists,
   constraining the values that can be used within the ``choices`` and
   ``default_targets`` parameters.

   As a frozen dataclass, instances of this class are immutable; their state
   cannot be changed after creation. Validation and normalization of inputs
   are performed automatically in the ``__post_init__`` method.

   .. attribute:: name

      The unique name for the reporter (e.g., 'rich-table').

      :type: str

   .. attribute:: description

      A short description of what the reporter does.

      :type: str

   .. attribute:: metrics

      The master set of metrics this reporter can handle.

      :type: frozenset[Metric]

   .. attribute:: targets

      The master set of targets this reporter can output to.

      :type: frozenset[Target]

   .. attribute:: default_targets

      The default subset of ``targets`` to use.

      :type: frozenset[Target]

   .. attribute:: formats

      The master set of formats this reporter can produce.

      :type: frozenset[Format]

   .. attribute:: choices

      Defines the reporter's command-line interface flags.

      :type: ChoicesConf

   .. attribute:: file_suffix

      The file extension for filesystem targets, without the leading dot.

      :type: str

   .. attribute:: file_unique

      If ``True``, generate a unique filename for each output.

      :type: bool

   .. attribute:: file_append

      If ``True``, append to the output file if it already exists.

      :type: bool

   .. attribute:: subdir

      The subdirectory for saved files; ``''`` means the root results directory.

      :type: str


   .. py:attribute:: ReporterConfig.choices
      :module: simplebench.reporters.reporter.config
      :type: ~simplebench.reporters.choices.choices_conf.ChoicesConf

      A :class:`~.ChoicesConf` object defining the reporter's command-line interface
      flags. These flags allow end-users to precisely control report generation by
      specifying which metrics to include, what output format to use, and where to
      send the report (targets). They can also control other reporter-specific options.


   .. py:attribute:: ReporterConfig.default_targets
      :module: simplebench.reporters.reporter.config
      :type: frozenset[~simplebench.enums.target.Target]

      The default subset of ``targets`` to use if not specified. Must be a subset of the
      main ``targets`` set.


   .. py:attribute:: ReporterConfig.description
      :module: simplebench.reporters.reporter.config
      :type: str

      A short description of what the reporter does. Cannot be empty or blank.


   .. py:attribute:: ReporterConfig.file_append
      :module: simplebench.reporters.reporter.config
      :type: bool

      If ``True``, append to the output file if it already exists.
      Mutually exclusive with ``file_unique``; exactly one must be ``True``.


   .. py:attribute:: ReporterConfig.file_suffix
      :module: simplebench.reporters.reporter.config
      :type: str

      The file extension to use for filesystem targets (e.g., 'txt'), without the leading dot.

      The suffix must consist only of alphanumeric characters and be 10 characters or less in length.


   .. py:attribute:: ReporterConfig.file_unique
      :module: simplebench.reporters.reporter.config
      :type: bool

      If ``True``, generate a unique filename for each output.
      Mutually exclusive with ``file_append``; exactly one must be ``True``.


   .. py:attribute:: ReporterConfig.formats
      :module: simplebench.reporters.reporter.config
      :type: frozenset[~simplebench.enums.format.Format]

      The master set of :class:`~.Format` enums this reporter can produce. This constrains
      the formats that can be used by any :class:`~.ChoiceConf` in the ``choices`` list.


   .. py:attribute:: ReporterConfig.name
      :module: simplebench.reporters.reporter.config
      :type: str

      The unique name for the reporter (e.g., 'rich-table'). Cannot be empty or blank.


   .. py:attribute:: ReporterConfig.metrics
      :module: simplebench.reporters.reporter.config
      :type: frozenset[~simplebench.enums.metric.Metric]

      The master set of :class:`~.Metric` enums this reporter can handle. This constrains
      the metrics that can be used by any :class:`~.ChoiceConf` in the ``choices`` list.


   .. py:attribute:: ReporterConfig.subdir
      :module: simplebench.reporters.reporter.config
      :type: str

      The subdirectory within the results directory to save files to. An empty string
      (``''``) specifies the root of the results directory (i.e., no subdirectory).

      A subdirectory path should only contain valid directory name elements separated by
      forward slashes (``'/'``). Each element must consist only of alphanumeric, underscore, or dash
