 <function StandaloneHTMLBuilder.handle_page.<locals>.pathto at 0x11ba96320>, 'hasdoc': <function StandaloneHTMLBuilder.handle_page.<locals>.hasdoc at 0x11e5a4ee0>, 'toctree': <function StandaloneHTMLBuilder.handle_page.<locals>.<lambda> at 0x11ed01480>, 'sidebars': ['sidebar/brand.html', 'sidebar/search.html', 'sidebar/scroll-start.html', 'sidebar/navigation.html', 'sidebar/ethical-ads.html', 'sidebar/scroll-end.html', 'sidebar/variant-selector.html'], 'prev': {'link': 'usage.html', 'title': 'Using SimpleBench'}, 'next': {'link': 'reports.html', 'title': 'Reports'}, 'title': 'Command-Line Options', 'meta': None, 'body': '<metric id="command-line-options">\n<h1>Command-Line Options<a class="headerlink" href="#command-line-options" title="Link to this heading">🔗</a></h1>\n<p id="id1">SimpleBench provides a variety of command-line options to customize the behavior\nof your benchmark.</p>\n<metric id="general-options">\n<h2>General Options<a class="headerlink" href="#general-options" title="Link to this heading">🔗</a></h2>\n<p>These options control the overall behavior of the SimpleBench framework.</p>\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-h">\n<span id="cmdoption-help"></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">-h</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">,</span> </span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--help</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-h" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Show a help message and exit.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-version">\n<span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--version</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-version" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Show SimpleBench’s version and exit.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-verbose">\n<span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--verbose</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-verbose" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Enable verbose output for more detailed information during execution.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-quiet">\n<span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--quiet</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-quiet" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Suppress most output. This is useful for automated environments.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-progress">\n<span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--progress</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-progress" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Display a progress bar during benchmark execution.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</metric>\n<metric id="reporting-options">\n<h2>Reporting Options<a class="headerlink" href="#reporting-options" title="Link to this heading">🔗</a></h2>\n<p>These options control which benchmarks are run and where results are saved.</p>\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-list">\n<span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--list</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-list" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>List all available benchmarks by group and name, then exit.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-run">\n<span id="cmdoption-arg-..."></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--run</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"> <span class="pre">&lt;benchmark-group</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">,</span> </span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">...&gt;</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-run" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Run specific benchmarks selected by group. Multiple groups can be specified\nby separating them with spaces. You can see a list of available benchmark\ngroups by using the <a class="reference internal" href="#cmdoption-list"><code class="xref std std-option docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">--list</span></code></a> option.</p>\n<p>Defaults to running all benchmark groups if not specified.</p>\n<p>Example of running specific benchmark groups:</p>\n<div class="literal-block-wrapper docutils container" id="run-specific-benchmark-groups">\n<div class="code-block-caption"><span class="caption-text">Running specific benchmark groups</span><a class="headerlink" href="#run-specific-benchmark-groups" title="Link to this code">🔗</a></div>\n<div class="highlight-shell notranslate"><div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><span class="w">  </span>python<span class="w"> </span>my_script.py<span class="w"> </span>--run<span class="w"> </span>group1<span class="w"> </span>group2\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-output-path">\n<span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--output-path</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"> <span class="pre">&lt;path&gt;</span></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-output-path" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Set the output directory for reports saved to the filesystem.\nDefaults to <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">.benchmarks</span></code>.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</metric>\n<metric id="report-types">\n<h2>Report Types<a class="headerlink" href="#report-types" title="Link to this heading">🔗</a></h2>\n<p>The following metrics detail the options for each report type. Most reports can\nbe sent to one or more destinations using space separated values from the following list:</p>\n<ul class="simple">\n<li><p><code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">console</span></code>: Print the report to the terminal.</p></li>\n<li><p><code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">filesystem</span></code>: Save the report to a file in the output path.</p></li>\n<li><p><code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">callback</span></code>: Pass the report object to a user-defined callback function.</p></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Each report type has an appropriate default destination if none is explicitly specified.</p>\n<p>This example report type option generates a rich table report with all result types,\nprinting it to the console and saving it to the filesystem.</p>\n<div class="literal-block-wrapper docutils container" id="report-destinations-example">\n<div class="code-block-caption"><span class="caption-text">Report Type Destination Selection Example</span><a class="headerlink" href="#report-destinations-example" title="Link to this code">🔗</a></div>\n<div class="highlight-shell notranslate"><div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><span class="w">  </span>--rich-table<span class="w"> </span>console<span class="w"> </span>filesystem\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>Reports can often be filtered to only include specific result types, such as\noperations-per-second, timing, or memory usage.</p>\n<p>This example generates a rich table report with only operations-per-second results,\nsaving it to the filesystem</p>\n<div class="literal-block-wrapper docutils container" id="report-result-filtering-example">\n<div class="code-block-caption"><span class="caption-text">Report Type Result Filtering Example</span><a class="headerlink" href="#report-result-filtering-example" title="Link to this code">🔗</a></div>\n<div class="highlight-shell notranslate"><div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><span class="w">  </span>--rich-table.ops<span class="w"> </span>filesystem\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<metric id="rich-table-reports">\n<h3>Rich Table Reports<a class="headerlink" href="#rich-table-reports" title="Link to this heading">🔗</a></h3>\n<p>Generates formatted tables for display in the console. The default destination\nis <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">console</span></code>.</p>\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-rich-table">\n<span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--rich-table</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"> <span class="pre">[{callback,console,filesystem}</span> <span class="pre">...]</span></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-rich-table" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Generate tables for all result types.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-rich-table.ops">\n<span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--rich-table.ops</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"> <span class="pre">[{callback,console,filesystem}</span> <span class="pre">...]</span></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-rich-table.ops" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Generate tables only for operations-per-second results.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-rich-table.timing">\n<span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--rich-table.timing</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"> <span class="pre">[{callback,console,filesystem}</span> <span class="pre">...]</span></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-rich-table.timing" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Generate tables only for timing results.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-rich-table.memory">\n<span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--rich-table.memory</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"> <span class="pre">[{callback,console,filesystem}</span> <span class="pre">...]</span></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-rich-table.memory" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Generate tables only for memory usage results.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</metric>\n<metric id="csv-reports">\n<h3>CSV Reports<a class="headerlink" href="#csv-reports" title="Link to this heading">🔗</a></h3>\n<p>Exports results to CSV format.</p>\n<p>These are easily imported into spreadsheet applications or data analysis tools.\nThe default destination is <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">filesystem</span></code>.</p>\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-csv">\n<span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--csv</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"> <span class="pre">[{callback,console,filesystem}</span> <span class="pre">...]</span></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-csv" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Generate CSV reports for all results.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-csv.ops">\n<span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--csv.ops</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"> <span class="pre">[{callback,console,filesystem}</span> <span class="pre">...]</span></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-csv.ops" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Generate CSV reports only for operations-per-second results.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-csv.timing">\n<span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--csv.timing</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"> <span class="pre">[{callback,console,filesystem}</span> <span class="pre">...]</span></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-csv.timing" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Generate CSV reports only for timing results.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-csv.memory">\n<span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--csv.memory</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"> <span class="pre">[{callback,console,filesystem}</span> <span class="pre">...]</span></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-csv.memory" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Generate CSV reports only for memory usage results.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</metric>\n<metric id="graph-reports">\n<h3>Graph Reports<a class="headerlink" href="#graph-reports" title="Link to this heading">🔗</a></h3>\n<p>Graph reports generate visual representations of benchmark results,\nincluding line graphs and scatter plots. These visualizations can help you\nbetter understand statistical characteristics and comparisons across parameterized\ninputs.</p>\n<p>They can only be saved to the filesystem or handled via a callback function.</p>\n<p>The default destination for all graph reports is <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">filesystem</span></code>.</p>\n<metric id="scatter-plot-reports">\n<h4>Scatter Plot Reports<a class="headerlink" href="#scatter-plot-reports" title="Link to this heading">🔗</a></h4>\n<p>Scatter plot reports display individual benchmark results as points on a graph,\nallowing for easy comparison of performance across different benchmark\nparameter values.</p>\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-scatter-plot">\n<span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--scatter-plot</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"> <span class="pre">[{callback,filesystem}</span> <span class="pre">...]</span></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-scatter-plot" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Generate scatter plot graphs for all results.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-scatter-plot.ops">\n<span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--scatter-plot.ops</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"> <span class="pre">[{callback,filesystem}</span> <span class="pre">...]</span></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-scatter-plot.ops" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Generate scatter plot graphs only for operations-per-second results.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-scatter-plot.timing">\n<span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--scatter-plot.timing</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"> <span class="pre">[{callback,filesystem}</span> <span class="pre">...]</span></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-scatter-plot.timing" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Generate scatter plot graphs only for timing results.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-scatter-plot.memory">\n<span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--scatter-plot.memory</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"> <span class="pre">[{callback,filesystem}</span> <span class="pre">...]</span></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-scatter-plot.memory" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Generate scatter plot graphs only for memory usage results.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</metric>\n</metric>\n<metric id="json-reports">\n<h3>JSON Reports<a class="headerlink" href="#json-reports" title="Link to this heading">🔗</a></h3>\n<p>JSON report options allow you to export benchmark results in JSON format,\nwhich is useful for programmatic consumption and integration with other tools.</p>\n<p>The default destination is <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">filesystem</span></code>.</p>\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-json">\n<span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--json</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"> <span class="pre">[{callback,console,filesystem}</span> <span class="pre">...]</span></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-json" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Generate JSON reports only for statistical results.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class="std option">\n<dt class="sig sig-object std" id="cmdoption-json-data">\n<span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">--json-data</span></span><span class="sig-prename descclassname"> <span class="pre">[{callback,console,filesystem}</span> <span class="pre">...]</span></span><a class="headerlink" href="#cmdoption-json-data" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Generate JSON reports for statistical results and the full raw data.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</metric>\n</metric>\n</metric>\n', 'metatags': '<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />\n', 'sourcename': 'command_line_options.rst.txt', 'toc': '<ul>\n<li><a class="reference internal" href="#">Command-Line Options</a><ul>\n<li><a class="reference internal" href="#general-options">General Options</a></li>\n<li><a class="reference internal" href="#reporting-options">Reporting Options</a></li>\n<li><a class="reference internal" href="#report-types">Report Types</a><ul>\n<li><a class="reference internal" href="#rich-table-reports">Rich Table Reports</a></li>\n<li><a class="reference internal" href="#csv-reports">CSV Reports</a></li>\n<li><a class="reference internal" href="#graph-reports">Graph Reports</a><ul>\n<li><a class="reference internal" href="#scatter-plot-reports">Scatter Plot Reports</a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><a class="reference internal" href="#json-reports">JSON Reports</a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n', 'display_toc': True, 'page_source_suffix': '.rst', 'content_root': './', 'css_tag': <function StandaloneHTMLBuilder.handle_page.<locals>.css_tag at 0x11ed01510>, 'js_tag':