cite>isinstance()</cite> and <cite>issubclass()</cite> checks.</p></li>\n<li><p><cite>is_choice()</cite>: A type-guard function to check if an object is a <cite>Choice</cite> instance.</p></li>\n<li><p><cite>SessionType</cite>: A lazy-loading proxy for the <cite>Session</cite> type that can be\nused in <cite>isinstance()</cite> and <cite>issubclass()</cite> checks.</p></li>\n<li><p><cite>is_session()</cite>: A type-guard function to check if an object is a <cite>Session</cite> instance.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class="py class">\n<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="simplebench.type_proxies.CaseTypeProxy">\n<em class="property"><span class="pre">class</span><span class="w"> </span></em><span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">simplebench.type_proxies.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">CaseTypeProxy</span></span><a class="reference internal" href="../_modules/simplebench/type_proxies/case_type_proxy.html#CaseTypeProxy"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#simplebench.type_proxies.CaseTypeProxy" title="Link to this definition">🔗</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class="reference internal" href="simplebench.type_proxies.lazy_type_proxy.html#simplebench.type_proxies.lazy_type_proxy.LazyTypeProxy" title="simplebench.type_proxies.lazy_type_proxy.LazyTypeProxy"><code class="xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">LazyTypeProxy</span></code></a>[<code class="xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">Case</span></code>]</p>\n<p>A special proxy class that acts like the <cite>Case</cite> type for runtime checks.</p>\n<p>It uses lazy loading to avoid circular import issues while still allowing\nruntime type checks and static type checking.</p>\n<p>It can be used in <cite>isinstance</cite> and <cite>issubclass</cite> checks as if it were\nthe actual <cite>Case</cite> type.</p>\n<div class="admonition warning">\n<p class="ad